            {
                "entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                "word": "tumbleweed",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2896e632-19d9-4a01-9499-823023fe000b",
                        "entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "tumbleweeds"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "19f43155-b55e-321a-a14e-94a8e87a777b",
                        "entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any plant which habitually breaks away from its roots once dry, forming a light, rolling mass which is driven by the wind from place to place; as Russian thistle, wild indigo, witch grass, Amaranthus albus, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6c69427e-fba8-34d4-b768-ab407b50004c",
                        "entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Describing unwanted silence and inactivity. Often used of a situation when one makes a statement that is ignored or ill-received by one's audience, as the resultant silence is likened to that of a desolate desert with rolling tumbleweeds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "attributive",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "833e41b9-4ea6-4dd5-8a75-8de0d1cd7f80",
                                "sense_id": "6c69427e-fba8-34d4-b768-ab407b50004c",
                                "text": "Putting an ad in the local paper that Spock's Beard and Arena are in town will get you a tumbleweed response and some wasted revenue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "499c4fe1-58d2-43d7-8c82-81275855dc66",
                                "sense_id": "6c69427e-fba8-34d4-b768-ab407b50004c",
                                "text": "“Why do families argue?” may only induce the tumbleweed response. (Could you answer that question out of the blue?)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8aa9414c-4c47-36c7-bf78-078a1036f193",
                        "entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tan colour, like that of a tumbleweed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a42b2a36-3888-48a6-902a-5eb3918cfe2a",
                        "source_entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                        "source_sense_description": "plant which breaks loose and is driven by the wind",
                        "target_lang_word": "tuimelkruid",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tuimelkruid",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7859a420-7e12-39bc-a4df-ec5cfbe64c69",
                                        "entry_id": "5db8478c-2459-3cc1-b28c-dc3acaf9b9ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "bovengronds deel van een plant met zaden of sporen, dat na verdroging afbreekt, door de wind gaat voortrollen en op die manier zorgt voor de verspreiding van nieuwe planten over een groter gebied"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea663564-2dfd-4d41-bf00-773875ac2179",
                                                "sense_id": "7859a420-7e12-39bc-a4df-ec5cfbe64c69",
                                                "text": "Een kurai is net zoiets als het ‘tumbleweed’ dat we uit de Amerikaanse western kennen: zo’n rondrollend struikje, het bovengrondse deel van een plant die ook bekendstaat als steppenroller of tuimelkruid en die voortbewogen door de wind zijn zaden verspreidt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b17ed63-236f-44b5-bb75-8259de0ef245",
                        "source_entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                        "source_sense_description": "plant which breaks loose and is driven by the wind",
                        "target_lang_word": "stepperoller",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ef417e9-0b5b-433d-a144-938f0f763b4a",
                        "source_entry_id": "35914e68-e253-3246-87c8-7a7c3ff3ffaa",
                        "source_sense_description": "plant which breaks loose and is driven by the wind",
                        "target_lang_word": "virevoltant",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "virevoltant",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "505ee9ff-560e-3c24-aef8-cfc234e19f2d",
                                        "entry_id": "f3982866-59de-3b3c-96b9-b6a1a1fcf690",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui virevolte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca839e23-1708-4294-8d44-cdf5c8fcc772",
                                                "sense_id": "505ee9ff-560e-3c24-aef8-cfc234e19f2d",
                                                "text": "Les sons virevoltants de la langue européenne à la mode, en le caressant, furent comme un baiser à son oreille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "008e5b9d-ea64-4c44-8231-5cbe99b8cb31",
                                                "sense_id": "505ee9ff-560e-3c24-aef8-cfc234e19f2d",
                                                "text": "Car Montpellier, hors la session universitaire où la nuée virevoltante des étudiants envahissait et rendait vie et bruyance, rompant avec la somnolence habituelle de ma douce et égocentrique ville, restait figée dans un train-train « pépère »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "virevoltant",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acfc9680-4aa4-3d76-84c8-08191ee64bac",
                                        "entry_id": "aa19deaf-7670-3df6-ae32-d668ca10f1e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Partie aérienne de certaines plantes des déserts du nord des États-Unis qui, une fois mûre et sèche, se sépare de la racine et peut se mettre à rouler au gré du vent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6a8c20e-f362-40cf-826d-119053cbad3f",
                                                "sense_id": "acfc9680-4aa4-3d76-84c8-08191ee64bac",
                                                "text": "Des virevoltants enflammés roulaient en tous sens à travers la cour, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5304165-e67f-48f6-9e0e-b4f3e9d2130f",
                                                "sense_id": "acfc9680-4aa4-3d76-84c8-08191ee64bac",
                                                "text": "Vous en avez sûrement déjà vu, ne serait-ce que dans un western. Vous savez, ce sont ces buissons ronds, desséchés, qui filent dans les rues des petites villes du grand Ouest américain, poussés par le vent. Là-bas, on les appelle des « tumbleweeds ». La traduction française décrit bien leur comportement : les « virevoltants ». Car ils roulent, vont et viennent, tournent, passent et repassent au gré de la brise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "virevoltant",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b2e8c17-6587-3df6-bb71-335dcb0f7c43",
                                        "entry_id": "2fb3c3fe-75d0-354b-b91d-8b25da48a351",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Participe présent de virevolter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f013dfb-9a05-4b90-be87-e5ba4f2d9008",
                                                "sense_id": "5b2e8c17-6587-3df6-bb71-335dcb0f7c43",
                                                "text": "Parmi les couples qui tournaient, il apercevait, fox-trottant, virevoltant, pleins d’allégresse et d’entrain, Charlotte et Béchoux"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
